    "originalInstructions": "1. Mix molasses with the spices in it and steep gently twenty or thirty minutes, not boiling hot\n2. Beat the eggs very lightly\n3. Flour the fruit well\n4. Dissolve soda in water\n5. Put the fruit in last, stirring it gradually and adding the dissolved soda\n6. Add flour after the fruit is in if necessary\n7. Butter a sheet of paper and lay it in the pan\n8. Lay in some slices of citron, then a layer of the mixture, then of citron again, etc., till the pan is nearly full\n9. Bake three or four hours, according to the thickness of the loaves, in a tolerably hot oven, and with steady heat\n10. Let it cool in the oven gradually\n11. Ice when cold",
